 Vector drawables, Material symbols, images and the world-clock city table,
 converted from AOSP and LineageOS sources (frameworks/base SystemUI,
 Launcher3, DeskClock, Dialer, Messaging, ExactCalculator).

Files: */po/*.po
Copyright: 2026 pulpoff <pashkovsky@gmail.com>
           The Android Open Source Project
           The LineageOS Project
License: Expat and Apache-2.0
Comment:
 The translations whose translator comment says "android: <app> <resource>"
 are that AOSP or LineageOS app's translations of the same English string
 (lineage-24.0, at the commits tools/i18n/android-sources.json pins), some of
 them adapted as the comment says; they are under the Apache License 2.0. The
 other translations are VibeOS's own, under the Expat licence.
 tools/i18n/NOTICE repeats the notice.

Files: apps/dialer/data/sounds/call-recording-en.opus
Copyright: Bryce Beattie (Piper voice en_GB-cori-high, rhasspy/piper-voices)
           Cori Samuel (the recordings, LibriVox)
License: Expat
Comment:
 The Phone's call-recording announcement in English, "This call is now being
 recorded", read by the Piper voice en_GB-cori-high (MIT) and made with
 apps/dialer/data/sounds/make-sounds.sh. The voice was trained from scratch on
 Cori Samuel's LibriVox recordings (https://librivox.org), which are in the
 public domain.

Files: apps/dialer/data/sounds/call-recording-de.opus
       apps/dialer/data/sounds/call-recording-es.opus
       apps/dialer/data/sounds/call-recording-nl.opus
       apps/dialer/data/sounds/call-recording-ru.opus
Copyright: Michael Hansen and the rhasspy/piper-voices contributors (Piper voices)
           Thorsten Müller (Thorsten-Voice)
License: Expat
Comment:
 The Phone's call-recording announcement in German, Spanish, Dutch and
 Russian, read by the Piper voices de_DE-thorsten-medium, es_ES-davefx-medium,
 nl_NL-pim-medium and ru_RU-denis-medium (MIT) and made with
 apps/dialer/data/sounds/make-sounds.sh. Their recordings are under CC0
 (Thorsten-Voice, https://github.com/thorstenMueller/Thorsten-Voice; the
 others https://github.com/OHF-Voice/voice-datasets), and the voices are
 trained from the Piper voice nl_BE-rdh-medium, whose recordings are CC0 too
 (https://github.com/r-dh/dutch-vl-tts).

Files: apps/dialer/data/sounds/call-recording-fr.opus
       apps/dialer/data/sounds/call-recording-it.opus
Copyright: Michael Hansen and the rhasspy/piper-voices contributors (Piper voices)
           Centre for Speech Technology Research, University of Edinburgh, and
           Idiap Research Institute (the SIWIS French Speech Synthesis Database)
           NVIDIA Corporation (the Hi-Fi Multi-Speaker English TTS Dataset)
License: Expat and CC-BY-4.0
Comment:
 The Phone's call-recording announcement in French and Italian, read by the
 Piper voices fr_FR-siwis-medium and it_IT-paola-medium (MIT) and made with
 apps/dialer/data/sounds/make-sounds.sh. The French voice is trained on the
 SIWIS French Speech Synthesis Database (CC BY 4.0,
 https://datashare.is.ed.ac.uk/handle/10283/2353), the Italian one on
 recordings under CC0 (https://github.com/OHF-Voice/voice-datasets); both are
 trained from the Piper voice en_US-hifi_tts_92-medium, the voice of Cori
 Samuel in NVIDIA's Hi-Fi Multi-Speaker English TTS Dataset (CC BY 4.0,
 https://www.openslr.org/109/).

